    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate prioritizing stolen base upside and high-leverage lineup slots. The primary cornerstone of our offense is **Trea Turner**, who commands our highest score (71.06) due to the perfect convergence of an elite 1.000 stolen base probability against a slow-delivery pitcher and a prime leadoff position. He is closely shadowed by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (77.01) and **Yordan Alvarez** (76.23). While **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits from a massive 14% boost due to favorable platoon dynamics, **Yordan Alvarez** remains a locked-in start regardless of matchup, bolstered by his elite 0.419 xwOBA. We are also expecting a significant contribution from **Christian Yelich** (75.84), who draws a favorable matchup against the high-xERA Roki Sasaki and benefits from a 13% platoon efficiency gain.\n\nThe decision to slot **Colt Keith** (68.51) and **Kyle Schwarber** (64.88) into the active roster was driven by their advantageous lineup spots, with both assuming roles at the top of their respective orders that maximize their plate appearance frequency against beatable arms like Brandon Young and Slade Cecconi. Our most difficult bench decision involved **Carson Benge** (51.97); while his 10% boost for hitting leadoff kept him relevant, he was ultimately eclipsed by the positional scarcity and higher-ceiling efficiency scores of our primary starters. We are continuing to monitor the status of **Junior Caminero**, whose potential output is currently neutralized by a rainout, while **Caleb Durbin**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, **Zac Veen**, **Lars Nootbaar**, **Josh Smith**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez** remain unavailable for selection due to minor league assignments, injury, or lack of confirmed lineup spots.\n\nManagement remains cautious regarding the wind conditions in the matchups for **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber**, where \"Wind In\" flags present a marginal risk to home run potential, offset only by their high-volume scoring projections. Conversely, **Chase Meidroth** (53.51) and **Casey Schmitt** (50.65) enjoy a 5% \"Wind Out\" boost, which acts as a stabilizer for their scores in otherwise mediocre matchups. All projected lineups remain \"Pending,\" so final game-day adjustments will be made the moment official cards are posted to ensure **Dillon Dingler**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Luke Raley**, and **Hyeseong Kim** maintain their projected platoon advantages.",
